{"entries":[{"id":"tsk-1pe-4-1","title":"1 Peter 4:1","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"1PE","chapterStart":4,"verseStart":1,"chapterEnd":4,"verseEnd":1},"content":"<p>1 He exhorts them to cease from sin by the example of Christ, and the consideration of the general end that now approaches; 12 and comforts them against persecution.</p>\n<p>Christ. 3:18 arm. Ro 13:12-14; Php 2:5; Heb 12:3 for. Ro 6:2,7,11; Ga 2:20; 5:24; Col 3:3-5 ceased. Isa 1:16; Eze 16:41; Heb 4:10</p>"},{"id":"tsk-1pe-4-2","title":"1 Peter 4:2","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"1PE","chapterStart":4,"verseStart":2,"chapterEnd":4,"verseEnd":2},"content":"<p>no. 2:1,14; Ro 7:4; 14:7; Eph 4:17,22-24; 5:7,8; Col 3:7,8; Tit 3:3-8 the lusts. Ho 6:7; *marg: Mr 7:21; Eph 2:3 the will. 2:15; Ps 143:10; Mt 7:21; 12:50; 21:31; Mr 3:35; Joh 1:13; 7:17 Ro 6:11; 12:2; 2Co 5:15; Ga 2:19,20; Eph 5:17; 6:6; Col 1:9; 4:12 1Th 5:18; Heb 13:21; Jas 1:18; 1Jo 2:17</p>"},{"id":"tsk-1pe-4-3","title":"1 Peter 4:3","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"1PE","chapterStart":4,"verseStart":3,"chapterEnd":4,"verseEnd":3},"content":"<p>the time. Eze 44:6; 45:9; Ac 17:30; Ro 8:12,13; 1Co 6:11 to have. 1:14; De 12:30,31; Ro 1:20-32; Eph 2:2,3; 4:17; 1Th 4:5; Tit 3:3 lasciviousness. Mr 7:22; 2Co 12:21; Ga 5:19; Eph 4:19; Jude 1:4 excess. 2Sa 13:28; Pr 23:29-35; Isa 5:11; 28:7; Eph 5:18 revellings. Ga 5:21 and. 1Ki 21:26; 2Ch 15:8; Isa 65:4; Jer 16:18; Re 17:4,5</p>"},{"id":"tsk-1pe-4-4","title":"1 Peter 4:4","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"1PE","chapterStart":4,"verseStart":4,"chapterEnd":4,"verseEnd":4},"content":"<p>excess. Mt 23:25; Lu 15:13; Ro 13:13; 2Pe 2:22 speaking. 2:12; 3:16; Ac 13:45; 18:6; 2Pe 2:12; Jude 1:10</p>"},{"id":"tsk-1pe-4-5","title":"1 Peter 4:5","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"1PE","chapterStart":4,"verseStart":5,"chapterEnd":4,"verseEnd":5},"content":"<p>shall. Mal 3:13-15; Mt 12:36; Lu 16:2; Ro 14:12; Jude